INT. CONVEYOR SORTING FLOOR - NIGHT

Parcels clatter down steel chutes. Yellow strobes spin.

POPPY (20s, high-vis vest, hair clip) slides a crate of sealed boxes onto the belt, eyes on the clock, while RHETT (30s, forklift jacket, toothpick) lifts a pallet with practiced ease, ZEKE (40s, supervisor, clipboard, comb-over) paces the mezzanine, TILDA (50s, scanner gun, glasses on a chain) calls out numbers, and MANNY (20s, headphones, tattoo of a swallow) hauls a cart toward the loading dock, each of them moving in a pattern they've rehearsed for weeks.

POPPY
Rhett, the third pallet.

RHETT
I see it, Poppy.

TILDA
(scanning)
Four-four-one-seven. Four-four-one-eight.

ZEKE
(from above)
Everybody smile! The auditor's coming at midnight!

MANNY
Tilda, is it the blue box?

TILDA
Wait for the nod.

Poppy bends over the blue box, lifts a corner. Inside, bricks of cash in plastic. Her pulse jumps. She closes the lid.

POPPY
(low)
Now.

The belt jolts and stops. Strobes die. Total dark.

A new voice, calm, from the stairs. OSWALD (60s, charcoal coat, a clip-on tie, a company badge) switches on a flashlight and sweeps it across them.

OSWALD
The auditor is early, I'm afraid.

Rhett's pallet crashes. Poppy runs. Manny runs. Tilda drops her scanner. Zeke whips around.

ZEKE
Oswald? Oswald, we can explain!

OSWALD
I'm sure you can, Zeke.
